---
import { Picture } from "astro:assets";
import { image, still } from "../data/catalog.ts";
import AppWindow from "./AppWindow.astro";
import Keycap from "./Keycap.astro";

const needs = still("workshop/needs-you");
const power = still("workshop/power");
const actions = ["attach", "stop", "summary", "new session here", "reveal folder", "copy path", "hide project", "star"];
---

<section class="band" id="drive" aria-labelledby="drive-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot" style="--tone:var(--needs-you)"></span> drive</p>
    <h2 id="drive-title">Then drive it from the map</h2>
    <p class="lead">
      Sessions live in Claude Code's own background daemon. Botropolis starts them, opens them in a terminal, parks them and wakes them, and never
      writes to <code>~/.claude</code> itself.
    </p>

    <div class="row">
      <AppWindow title="botropolis — workshop">
        <Picture src={image(needs.image)} formats={["avif"]} fallbackFormat="webp" widths={[640, 960, 1280, 1920]} sizes="(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 760px" alt={needs.description} loading="lazy" />
      </AppWindow>
      <div class="text">
        <h3>{needs.title}</h3>
        <p><Keycap k="tab" /> jumps to the next session waiting on an answer and opens its card. <Keycap k="enter" /> attaches it.</p>
        <ul class="chips" aria-label="Card actions">
          {actions.map((a) => <li>{a}</li>)}
        </ul>
        <p class="note">
          A card's summary shows the recap Claude Code writes when a session is left waiting. Asking for a fresh one is the only thing on the map that
          spends tokens, and only when you press it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row flip">
      <AppWindow title="botropolis — power plant">
        <Picture src={image(power.image)} formats={["avif"]} fallbackFormat="webp" widths={[640, 960, 1280, 1920]} sizes="(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 760px" alt={power.description} loading="lazy" />
      </AppWindow>
      <div class="text">
        <h3>{power.title}</h3>
        <p>Click the power plant for the breakdown by model, project and session over an hour, a day or a week. Its wires carry each session's live token rate.</p>
        <p class="note">Costs are estimates, which is why they carry a ~.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  code {
    font: 0.92em var(--mono);
  }
  .row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.7fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 40px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .row + .row {
    margin-top: 72px;
  }
  .flip > :first-child {
    order: 2;
  }
  h3 {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .text p {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  .note {
    color: var(--dim);
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .chips {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .chips li {
    padding: 5px 9px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: #2a2d34;
    color: var(--accent);
    font: 500 13px/1 var(--font);
  }
  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .row {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 24px;
    }
    .flip > :first-child {
      order: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
